    <!-- Guide -->
    <string name="guide_title">Guide</string>
    <string name="guide_best_title">What works best</string>
    <string name="guide_best_body">There is no official formula: Weappy has never published one, and demand also depends on ads, holidays, competition and scandals. The most efficient routine players report is to start from a method, then feed the game’s real attendance back in after every week. The planner rescales all remaining weeks to what your movie actually draws, so you stop renting empty cinemas.</string>
    <string name="guide_routine_title">Weekly routine</string>
    <string name="guide_step_1">Before release, enter the scores and your own screenings, pick a method and book weeks 1–4 as shown.</string>
    <string name="guide_step_2">After each week, open the distribution results in the game and copy Screenings and Attendance into that week.</string>
    <string name="guide_step_3">Book the next weeks with the recalibrated numbers. At 97 % attendance or more the week sold out, so book a little more.</string>
    <string name="guide_step_4">For weeks 5 and later, use Setup distribution rather than Extend, and avoid renting unless the movie still grosses well.</string>
    <string name="guide_methods_title">Methods compared</string>
    <string name="guide_method_steam">The formula V1 used. Gentle −20 % decay, so later weeks are the most generous. Fine when your own cinemas cover them, costly when you rent.</string>
    <string name="guide_method_fast">Newest community guideline (Apr–Jun 2026). Week 2 is about 60 % of week 1, then it halves; week 5 is about 12 % of week 1. Closest to the attendance drop players report (about 90, 45, 20 then 15 %).</string>
    <string name="guide_method_two_thirds">A middle ground: −1/3 every week from a commercial ×2 start.</string>
    <string name="guide_method_custom">Fit your own studio once you have a few releases of real attendance.</string>
    <string name="guide_patch_title">Patch notes that matter</string>
    <string name="guide_patch_073">0.8.73EA · 21 Oct 2026 · Latest build. No distribution change.</string>
    <string name="guide_patch_071">0.8.71EA · 7 May 2026 · Cinema maintenance is no longer free: owning cinemas now has a running cost.</string>
    <string name="guide_patch_067">0.8.67EA · 27 Jan 2026 · Slightly more money from distribution. Rivals buy cinemas more aggressively.</string>
    <string name="guide_patch_xmas">Christmas Update · 18 Dec 2025 · Christmas joins the release calendar.</string>
    <string name="guide_patch_0505">0.8.50.5EA · 22 Aug 2025 · Holiday attendance boost +50 %. Scandals hurt attendance less.</string>
    <string name="guide_patch_act2">Act 2 · closed beta from 8 Dec 2026 · Studios lose their cinemas and distributors appear. These methods will need revisiting then.</string>
